# Gate D digest safety.
#
# The Gate D acceptance marker binds a SHA-256 computed over the *bytes on disk* of the
# frozen generator files. Git's autocrlf/eol conversion can silently rewrite those bytes
# (LF <-> CRLF) without `git status` reporting anything, which changes the digest and
# closes the training lock. That happened once during this round to
# research/tree_qc/gate_d_sampler.py and was recovered from the stored blob.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for the frozen research core so a checkout
# can never rewrite it again. The files are stored and checked out exactly as committed.
research/tree_qc/gate_d_provenance.py  -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_scene.py       -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_geometry.py    -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_generator.py   -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_sampler.py     -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_dataset.py     -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_metrics.py     -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_train.py       -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_fingerprint.py -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_diagnostic.py  -text
research/tree_qc/gate_d_lock.py        -text
research/tree_qc/reports/GATE_D_ACCEPTANCE.json -text
